<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Vehicle Financial Decision Engine</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #edf3f2;
      --card: #ffffff;
      --text: #243f4d;
      --muted: #4e5f68;
      --accent1: #214b5b;
      --accent2: #2e9f96;
      --border: #dfe8e6;
      --shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(22, 42, 51, 0.08);
      --radius: 18px;
      --maxw: 1180px;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: #1f2933;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .navbar {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 1000;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.96);
      backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .nav-inner {
      max-width: var(--maxw);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 18px 24px;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .brand {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: var(--text);
      letter-spacing: 0.3px;
    }

    .nav-links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 26px;
    }

    .nav-links a {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--text);
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: 0.98rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.3px;
    }

    .section {
      max-width: var(--maxw);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 18px 24px 0;
    }

    .hero {
      margin-top: 18px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent1), var(--accent2));
      color: white;
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      min-height: 390px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      text-align: center;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      padding: 40px 28px;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
      line-height: 1.18;
      font-weight: 800;
    }

    .hero .meta {
      margin-top: 22px;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    .hero .meta p {
      margin: 8px 0;
    }

    .card {
      background: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      padding: 28px 30px;
      margin: 24px 0;
    }

    .card h2 {
      margin-top: 0;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 2rem;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    .card h3 {
      color: var(--text);
      margin-top: 0;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      color: #2d3742;
    }

    .grid-2 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 28px;
    }

    .pill-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 16px;
    }

    .pill {
      background: #eef7f6;
      color: var(--text);
      border: 1px solid #d7e9e6;
      padding: 8px 14px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    ul.clean, ol.clean {
      padding-left: 22px;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .stat-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 16px;
      margin-top: 18px;
    }

    .stat {
      background: #f6fbfa;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 18px;
    }

    .stat strong {
      display: block;
      font-size: 1.55rem;
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }

    .footer {
      max-width: var(--maxw);
      margin: 10px auto 40px;
      padding: 0 24px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .footer a {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .grid-2, .stat-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .nav-inner {
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: flex-start;
      }

      .nav-links {
        gap: 14px 18px;
      }

      .hero {
        min-height: 320px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="navbar">
    <div class="nav-inner">
      <div class="brand">Vehicle Financial Decision Engine</div>
      <nav class="nav-links">
        <a href="#home">HOME</a>
        <a href="#summary">PROJECT SUMMARY</a>
        <a href="#data">DATA SOURCES</a>
        <a href="#findings">FINDINGS</a>
        <a href="#impact">BROADER IMPACTS</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="section" id="home">
      <div class="hero">
        <div>
          <h1>Vehicle Financial Decision Engine</h1>
          <div class="meta">
            <p><strong>Group ID:</strong> 20</p>
            <p><strong>Members:</strong> Nyi Wai Yan Tun, Sana Al Hamimidi</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="summary">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Project Summary</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          This project helps car buyers make smarter financial decisions by looking beyond the listed price of a vehicle.
          The platform focuses on long-term financial effects like depreciation, insurance-related cost context, and
          region-based market behavior across California.
        </p>
        <p>
          A major idea behind this project is that vehicle value does not change the same way everywhere. A truck may hold
          value better in one region while losing value faster in another. Because of that, the website is designed to let
          users compare depreciation patterns across regions and understand how geography affects the long-term value of a car.
        </p>
        <p>
          The system is also planned to use machine learning to assign each vehicle a depreciation rating out of 5, helping
          users compare vehicles in a way that is easier to understand.
        </p>
        <div class="pill-row">
          <span class="pill">California market focus</span>
          <span class="pill">Regional depreciation analysis</span>
          <span class="pill">Vehicle comparison</span>
          <span class="pill">ML-based rating system</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="stat-grid">
        <div class="stat"><strong>8</strong><span>datasets combined for the project</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>50,614</strong><span>California vehicle listings after filtering</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>26</strong><span>columns in the original vehicles dataset</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>5-star</strong><span>planned depreciation rating scale</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="data">
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Data Sources</h3>
          <ol class="clean">
            <li><strong>vehicles.csv</strong> — Craigslist vehicle listings used for California resale analysis.</li>
            <li><strong>vehicle fuel-type registration datasets</strong> — annual registration data by zip code and fuel type in California.</li>
            <li><strong>car_data.csv</strong> — vehicle MSRP and pricing data used to help estimate depreciation behavior.</li>
            <li><strong>Insurance expenditure data</strong> — state-level cost context for ownership.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Core Features Used</h3>
          <ul class="clean">
            <li>Region and zip-code based demand</li>
            <li>Price, year, and odometer</li>
            <li>Manufacturer, model, condition, fuel, type, and size</li>
            <li>Registration trends and geographic market differences</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="findings">
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Preliminary Findings</h3>
          <ul class="clean">
            <li>Newer vehicles tend to list for higher prices.</li>
            <li>Higher mileage is linked to lower prices.</li>
            <li>Top registered brands also appear among the most listed used cars in California.</li>
            <li>Regional demand likely plays a meaningful role in resale value.</li>
            <li>Fuel type alone is not enough; vehicle type also matters when studying depreciation.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Questions the Project Tries to Answer</h3>
          <ul class="clean">
            <li>How does geography within California affect depreciation?</li>
            <li>Which vehicle features most influence resale value over time?</li>
            <li>What combination of price, interest rate, demand, and location gives the best long-term value?</li>
            <li>Which vehicle segments keep a more stable depreciation curve across regions?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="impact">
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Broader Impacts</h3>
          <p>
            This project can help first-time buyers, students, seniors, and budget-conscious families understand the hidden
            long-term cost of owning a car. It can also help gig drivers and small dealerships make smarter decisions using
            clearer market signals.
          </p>
          <p>
            By turning complicated financial patterns into simple visual comparisons, the platform supports better planning,
            better negotiation, and better value for buyers over time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>GitHub Pages Notes</h3>
          <p>To publish this on GitHub Pages later, keep the project simple:</p>
          <ol class="clean">
            <li>Save this file as <strong>index.html</strong>.</li>
            <li>Push it to a GitHub repository.</li>
            <li>Open <strong>Settings → Pages</strong>.</li>
            <li>Select the main branch and root folder.</li>
            <li>GitHub will generate your public site link.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <p>
      Built for a class project. Replace this starter text with your final charts, screenshots, and model results before submission.
    </p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
